WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.650
- So pretend you're this guy

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.140
and you were really productive
earlier in the month.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.690
In fact, you were kind of killing it.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.430
You're reading lots of books,
hitting the gym consistently,

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.760
and actually getting your work in on time.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.910
But then something happened,

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.040
maybe you woke up on the
wrong side of the bed,

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.040
maybe an invisible demon ghost
violated you in your sleep.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.250
Whatever the case may be,

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.810
everything seems just a bit harder to do.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:21.660
You're tired.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.890
You've lost all the motivation you had

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.160
to keep being awesome.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.160
And you can't even remember
why you were being productive

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.060
in the first place.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.950
And that mental clarity that you seemed

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.290
to be the beneficiary of just yesterday,

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.010
seems to have ran away in the night.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.950
And unfortunately this
lack of motivation starts

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.950
to seep into the other areas of your life.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.810
The thought dawns on you to go to the gym

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:45.260
and you're too lazy to do it.
So you skip the gym that day.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.290
One day turns into two days,
two days turns into a week.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.380
You're also starting
to buy more junk food,

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.030
watch more TV, play more video games.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.880
And not only are you not doing the things

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.760
you know you should be doing,
but you don't even want to.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.340
You can't even remember why
you were being productive

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.330
in the first place.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.250
Why are we still here?

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.380
For a lot of people, these long
periods of success followed

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.990
by long periods of self destruction

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:11.350
and failure seem to be a common pattern.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.480
And while this issue is a
deep psychological issue

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.610
that I'll dive into in a later video,

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:19.320
I wanted to give you guys
a more practical guide

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.430
as to how I get myself out of these type

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.840
of pseudo depressive ruts and
start being productive again.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.500
Now, before we dive into these
really powerful strategies,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.920
I just wanna preface the
video with a couple of things.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.590
Number one is that this video is not meant

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.130
to be a replacement for going to therapy

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.520
if you actually have clinical depression.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.400
I'm not a doctor, I'm just a dude,

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.660
and I talk about what works for me.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.450
Second of all, even though this video

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.860
is about how to get out of a
rut efficiently or quickly,

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:49.040
that's all relative.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.690
You're usually not gonna
get out of a rut overnight.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.640
Okay, so strategy number one is to utilize

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.140
the do something principle.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.970
This principle is the catalyst for action.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.490
If you don't have the
motivation to do something,

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.800
you need something that'll
spark some sort of action,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.670
something to get the momentum going,

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:08.120
something to get the ball rolling.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.270
And the do something principle
is a means to take action

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.800
when you don't have the
motivation to do anything.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.170
So most people think that
in order to take action

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.630
on anything, you need to
be motivated to do that.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.600
And motivation comes when
you're inspired by something.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.820
So for instance, say
you're browsing Reddit

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:28.120
or something and you come
across a Matt D'Avella video

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.720
and by the end, he says
something that strikes a chord

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.260
with you and you're
inspired to take action.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.860
That inspiration served
as the adequate motivation

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.750
to take action on your goals.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.450
But to do something principle
dictates that inspiration,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.970
motivation, action is
not a linear sequence.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.360
It's an endless loop and you can start

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.590
wherever you wanna start.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.790
So it's far more efficient
to start with action

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.620
and let that action become the inspiration

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.160
and the motivation necessary
to take further action.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.010
So you may be thinking, thanks genius,

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.270
if I'm unmotivated to do something,

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.550
then I should just do something,
that's really helpful.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.210
But you actually take action

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.240
without motivation all the time.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.880
Do you need some sort of
huge inspirational epiphany

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.950
to take a shower? No, it's
just something you do.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.760
These monotonous actions
are the very actions

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.303
you should be using as momentum
to take further action.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.860
If you're just sitting there
waiting for inspiration

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.500
to strike you, go brush your teeth.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.300
Brushing your teeth is a
little constructive action

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.070
that will give you momentum
into taking further action.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:34.080
If you have to write a giant
essay, don't think to yourself,

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.460
oh, I have to go and write
my giant 4,000-word essay.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:39.900
Just say, I'm gonna open up the word doc,

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.400
write whatever comes to
my mind for one minute.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.860
And that's it. That's all I have to do.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.140
But once you start writing,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.930
you will tend to want to write more

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.150
because you've convinced
yourself to get there.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.600
That is in essence to
do something principle.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.240
Now, strategy number two
seems counter-intuitive

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.330
to what I just said,

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.360
and that is to reward
yourself for small wins.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.200
Now, if you follow this channel at all,

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.360
I am not a pat yourself on the back

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.630
and everyone gets an award kind of guy.

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:05.950
So if you're in the same boat,

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.230
but you might cringe at the
thought of rewarding yourself

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.780
for taking a shower or
something like that,

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:12.950
because you know you're
capable of so much more,

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.780
but the need to reward
yourself for small wins,

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.730
especially if you're in
a vulnerable situation

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.000
is a psychological necessity.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.770
And it has everything to do with the fact

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:25.050
that you have basically
two sides of your brain.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.470
And I'm not talking about right and left,

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:29.440
I'm talking more about the
more primal part of your brain,

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.780
which is closer to the stem

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.690
which is responsible for motivation

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.870
and emotion and stuff like that.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.410
And your more logical,
abstract, moralistic part

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.160
of your brain, which is present more

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.630
in the prefrontal cortex.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.730
So if your prefrontal cortex knows to use

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.730
the do something principle
in order to convince

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.520
your primal side of your brain
to take action on something,

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.350
it's important that you're
not too iron-fisted with this

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.430
because it's a negotiation with yourself.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.570
Don't be a slave driver to
the primal side of your brain

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.430
or your primal side of your
brain won't feel listened to,

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.420
it'll lash out and it
won't wanna do anything

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.870
that your logical side of
your brain wants it to do.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.350
So you almost need to
use your higher judgment

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.880
to provide compassionate guidance

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.830
to the primal part of your brain

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.770
and very gradually win it over.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.210
If you're too lazy to pretty
much do anything other

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.510
than sit around all day

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.240
and you use the do something principle

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:22.240
to convince your primal side of your brain

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:24.430
to brush your teeth, take a shower,

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.830
get some nice clothes on
and clean your kitchen

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.340
and you start to get really tired

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.820
and agitated after this, take a break.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:33.370
It may sound suspect and your logical side

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.060
of your brain knows
that you should be doing

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.290
a lot more than that.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.220
Just take it easy,

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:40.060
reward yourself for doing
something constructive for once

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.080
after days of bingeing dopamine,

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.730
and just relax and have a good time.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:44.710
So you might be thinking,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.720
how the heck am I supposed
to get out of a rut

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.690
if I don't ride this
momentum out into the sunset?

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.860
That's what tip number three is all about.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:56.180
So strategy number three is
all about progressive overload.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.930
It's very similar to the
philosophy of lifting weights

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.020
and getting stronger.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.470
Instead of yo-yoing between
taking crazy amounts of action

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.280
and then your primal brain lashing out

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.700
and going into long periods
of self-destruction,

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:11.150
you should be massaging yourself
into organically growing

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.790
a lifestyle that you
gradually get used to,

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.130
that's more and more productive,

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.100
and you do more and more every
day while rewarding yourself

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.670
for the small wins and comparing yourself

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.710
to who you were yesterday rather than

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.040
who someone else is today.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.320
So for instance, if you develop
a game plan over the course

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.910
of seven days to get out of a rut,

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.750
that's a lot more
realistic than just trying

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.280
to be productive all of a sudden.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.850
So say day one, you can't
really do much other

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.340
than go on the internet
for long periods of time.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.240
On this day, if you convince yourself

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.990
to take pretty much any
sort of constructive action,

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.750
that should be sufficient for the day.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.200
Day one should just be
about gradually taking

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.560
a little bit more action
and being happy with that.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.050
And the next day, remind
yourself that that wasn't so bad

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.070
and it actually felt
pretty good to take action

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.410
and try to do a little bit more.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.270
And if you do this day after day,

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.240
then gradually and organically,

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.590
both sides of your brain
will be in agreeance.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:05.000
And you'll very comfortably
start to rise from the ashes

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.400
like a phoenix and become the person

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.400
that you were earlier in that month.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.240
I can't stress how important this is,

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.650
managing expectations,
being patient with yourself

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:17.270
and letting your higher
faculties be very communicative

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.800
with the more primal and
emotional sides of your brain.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:23.150
This synergy between both
sides of your brain is integral

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.830
for maintaining long-term success.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:29.040
And you can eventually be
very reliably and sustainably,

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.210
living the kind of life

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.820
that you've always wanted to be living.

